    "cover": {
      "coverFields": {
        "coverPaymentTerms": "1. Mobilization Downpayment: A fifteen percent (15%) advance payment upon contract signing and receipt of Notice to Proceed (NTP), deductible pro-rata from each progress billing.\n\n2. Monthly Progress Billings: Progress billings shall be submitted on a monthly cut-off cycle reflecting actual physical accomplishment validated through joint site quantity measurements.\n\n3. Applicable Rates & Inclusions: Billing valuation shall apply the approved Bill of Quantities (BOQ) unit rates, inclusive of direct costs, equipment overhead, contractor profit, and applicable tax/VAT treatments.\n\n4. Retention Guarantee: A ten percent (10%) retention fee shall be deducted from each progress payment, to be released upon final turnover, completion of punchlist items, and issuance of Certificate of Final Acceptance.\n\n5. Invoicing & Settlement: All validated billing invoices shall be processed and settled within fifteen (15) calendar days from receipt of billing statement.",
        "coverQuotationDuration": "1. Validity Period: This commercial proposal and its corresponding unit rates remain firm and valid for thirty (30) calendar days from the date of submission.\n\n2. Cost Basis: Rates are strictly calculated based on Direct Unit Price Analysis (DUPA), prevailing material supplier rates, and current statutory labor wage orders.\n\n3. Adjustment Upon Expiry: Acceptance after the 30-day validity window shall be subject to mutual re-evaluation and adjustment based on published material price indexes and prevailing market conditions.",
        "coverProjectDuration": "1. Contract Duration: The total project completion period is estimated at 5 Calendar Days (approx. 4 Working Days, based on a 6-day work week), commencing within seven (7) calendar days from receipt of Notice to Proceed (NTP) and site possession.\n\n2. Milestone Schedule Baseline: A detailed CPM Gantt Chart and S-Curve progress baseline shall be submitted prior to mobilization and shall govern critical milestone tracking.\n\n3. Extension of Time (EOT): Excusable delays—including force majeure, unworkable weather beyond statistical averages, client-directed scope revisions, or delayed owner approvals—shall entitle the Contractor to an equitable extension of time without penalty.\n\n4. Substantial Completion & Handover: Substantial completion shall be declared when works are at least 95% complete and safely serviceable for their intended purpose, subject only to punchlist item rectifications.",
        "coverSpecialConditions": "1. Site & Plan Verification: This proposal is subject to final joint site verification of benchmarks, elevations, boundary monuments, and actual field conditions.\n\n2. Change Orders & Scope Variations: Any additions, deductions, or scope deviations from the approved BOQ shall be priced using the established DUPA cost factors and approved in writing prior to execution.\n\n3. Quantity Variance Threshold: Should actual site quantities deviate by more than fifteen percent (15%) from the estimated BOQ quantities through no fault of the Contractor, unit rates for the affected variance may be equitably renegotiated.\n\n4. Work Hours & Accelerated Work: Work shall proceed during standard permitted construction hours (Monâ€“Sat, 8:00 AM â€“ 5:00 PM). Overtime or night shift operations requested by the Client for schedule acceleration shall be subject to mutual agreement and night differential reimbursement.",
        "coverExcludedItems": "1. Specific Works Not Included in Contract: Any scope of work, trade discipline, or task not explicitly scheduled and priced in the approved Bill of Quantities (BOQ) is deemed excluded from the Contractor's contractual scope.\n\n2. Owner-Supplied Materials (OSM): Any specialized decorative fixtures, client-specified specialty equipment, or materials designated as Owner-Supplied shall be furnished directly by the Client at their expense.\n\n3. Works Executed by Other Contractors (as identified in BOQ): The following packages marked as \"By other Contractor\" in the BOQ shall be carried out directly by the Client's other independent contractors and are excluded from this contract: [03.01.04.00] Steel Structures (bolts, Plates, I Beams) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor).\n\n4. Government Permits & Assessment Fees: Building permits, occupancy clearances, fire safety inspection fees, zoning clearances, and local government assessment fees (unless explicitly itemized in the approved BOQ).\n\n5. Permanent Utility Infrastructure: Permanent electric transformer installations/tapping fees, permanent water meter connection charges, and permanent sewer connection fees assessed by utility concessionaires.\n\n6. Specialist Engineering & Off-Site Works: Geotechnical soil investigations, seismic soundness audits, structural retrofitting of existing adjacent structures, and civil works outside the designated property boundaries.",
        "coverClientMaterials": "1. Supply & Delivery: All Owner-Supplied Materials (OSM) and client-furnished equipment shall be delivered to the jobsite freight-prepaid, properly crated, and aligned with the agreed project procurement timeline.\n\n2. Quality & Specifications: The Client warrants that all OSM comply with project engineering specifications, building codes, and manufacturer quality standards.\n\n3. Site Handling & Storage: The Contractor shall provide reasonable protection and secure storage for OSM upon turnover, exercising standard care against loss or weather damage.\n\n4. Delivery Delays & Compensation: Any delay in OSM turnover, defective materials requiring replacement, or manufacturer shortages impacting the critical path shall entitle the Contractor to a day-for-day time extension and reimbursement of verified standby labor/equipment costs.",
        "coverOtherContractors": "1. Designated Works by Other Contractors: The following trade packages marked in the BOQ as \"By other Contractor\" shall be executed by the Client's other independent contractors: [03.01.04.00] Steel Structures (bolts, Plates, I Beams) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor).\n\n2. Protection of Installed Works: Independent trade contractors must respect completed works. Any damage inflicted onto finished finishes, MEPF lines, or waterproofing shall be rectified at the Client's expense.\n\n3. Shared Hoisting & Temporary Power: Access to vertical hoisting equipment, craneage, temporary power, and staging yards must be scheduled in advance with the Contractor's project superintendent.\n\n4. Performance & Liability Disclaimer: The Contractor assumes no liability for operational failures, schedule delays, or warranty liabilities originating from works performed by the Client's independent trade contractors.",
        "coverSubmittedBy": "",
        "coverSubmittedPosition": "",
        "coverAcceptedBy": "",
        "coverAcceptedPosition": "",
        "coverDocTitle": "CONSTRUCTION COST PROPOSAL",
        "coverDocNo": "FM-OPN-01-06",
        "coverRevNo": "Rev. No. 0",
        "coverEffectiveDate": "7/2/2026",
        "sbCoverPaperSize": "A4",
        "sbCoverOrientation": "portrait",
        "coverKeyDeliverables": "1. [01.00.00.00] PRELIMINARY FOR CIVIL WORKS: Comprehensive supply of materials, labor, specialized equipment, and engineering supervision for Project Management and Coordination, Facility Services Coordination, Construction Progress Reporting, Health and Safety provisions, and associated works, fully compliant with project plans and specifications.\n\n2. [02.00.00.00] Earth Works & Sub Structures: Comprehensive supply of materials, labor, specialized equipment, and engineering supervision for RETAINING WALL, Foundation Excavation, Earth Disposal, Retaining Wall Footing, and associated works, fully compliant with project plans and specifications.\n\n3. [03.00.00.00] STRUCTURAL WORKS: Comprehensive supply of materials, labor, specialized equipment, and engineering supervision for CONCRETE WORKS, FDN-GF - Concrete works, Steel Structures (bolts, Plates, I Beams) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor) (By other Contractor), GF-2F - Concrete works, and associated works, fully compliant with project plans and specifications.",
        "coverMethodologies": "1. Mobilization & Health/Safety Protocols: Rapid deployment of equipment, construction safety barriers, PPE enforcement, and securing required building clearances prior to breaking ground in full compliance with DOLE DO-13 standards.\n\n2. Substructure & Civil Execution: Systematic excavation guided by optical laser benchmarks, rigorous soil sub-grade verification, and controlled backfill compaction with field density testing (FDT) prior to concrete footing placement.\n\n3. Structural Reinforced Concrete Works: Pre-pour joint inspections checking rebar lap splices, spacing, and concrete cover chairs; continuous slump testing on site; and mandatory 7-day, 14-day, and 28-day laboratory concrete cylinder compressive strength tests.\n\n4. Quality Assurance & Final Turnover: Multi-tier quality audits with the Project Manager, systematic rectification of snag lists, handover of complete As-Built drawings, and turnover of manufacturer warranty certificates.",
        "sbCoverDurationDays": "5",
        "sbCoverWorkingDays": "4",
        "sbCoverDurationBasis": "6-day",
        "coverAttachedDocuments": "1. Detailed Bill of Quantities (BOQ): Itemized unit rates, material costs, labor rates, equipment rentals, and statutory markups.\n\n2. Project Schedule & Milestone Baseline: CPM Gantt Chart and S-Curve cash-flow progress projections.\n\n3. Technical Specifications & Material Schedule: Engineering specifications, brand standards, and material submittal schedules.\n\n4. Reference Drawings & Site Attachments: Architectural plans, schematic diagrams, site inspection photos, and reference documents attached to this proposal."
      },
      "editableHtml": [
        "CONSTRUCTION COST PROPOSAL",
        "FM-OPN-01-06",
        "Rev. No. 0",
        "7/2/2026",
        "Dear Sir/Madam,",
        "We are pleased to submit our cost proposal for the above-mentioned project for your review and consideration.",
        "This proposal has been prepared based on the project requirements, applicable scope of works, and the Summary of Bill of Quantities. The submitted amount reflects the estimated construction cost, including the required materials, labor, equipment, applicable multiplier factors for overhead cost and profit, and <span id=\"coverVatText1\">Non-VAT</span> or Non-VAT treatment as determined by the BOQ Summary. The complete Bill of Quantities (BOQ), Work Schedule / Gantt Chart, Technical Specifications, and supporting documents are attached hereto and form an integral part of this proposal.",
        "The cost breakdown by main category is presented below. The amounts shown represent the total cost per category, including all applicable adjustments for overhead, profit, and <span id=\"coverVatText2\">Non-VAT</span> as derived from the BOQ cost factors. Any revision in scope, specifications, quantity, site condition, or client instruction may require corresponding adjustment to the proposal amount.",
        "We trust that this submission meets your requirements. Should you need any clarification or additional information, we will be pleased to provide the necessary details.",
        "Thank you for the opportunity to submit this proposal. We look forward to your favorable review and approval.",
        "Respectfully yours,",
        "Confidentiality notice: No part of this document may be copied, reproduced, disclosed, or distributed to any third party—including other contractors, consultants, or suppliers—without the prior written consent of FCLDC. Unauthorized use, duplication, or sharing of this proposal in any form is strictly prohibited."
      ],
